# Attachment upload = encrypt.lu single PUT (find the delta)

encrypt.lu proves Safari can PUT ~22–100 MiB in one XHR when the hop is equivalent.
Do **not** treat “Safari needs chunks” as the main story.

## Primary recipe (always on)

| Requirement | Value |
|---|---|
| Page | `https://privatenote.ai` (prod A/B); staging QA: `https://premium.privatenote.ai` |
| Upload | `https://upload.privatenote.ai` / `https://upload-staging.privatenote.ai` |
| Transport | **XHR** `xhr.send(Blob)` (never Safari `fetch` for the binary PUT) |
| Body | one Blob `{ type: "application/octet-stream" }` |
| Method | PUT `/api/notes/:id/file` |
| Auth | **`Authorization: Bearer {uploadToken}`** (primary). Query `?uploadToken=` is client fallback only. |
| Headers | Do **not** set `Content-Type` / `Content-Length` from JS for Blob PUTs |
| Credentials | omit / `withCredentials` false |
| Proxy | never Pages `/api` for the binary body |

## CORS (upload relay)

Match `relay.encrypt.lu`: echo Origin, **echo `Access-Control-Request-Headers`**, Allow-Methods GET/POST/PUT/OPTIONS, Max-Age 86400, allow `Authorization` + `Content-Length`, **no** Allow-Credentials, **no** Set-Cookie.

## Fast A/B (do this once)

Same Mac Safari, same ~22 MiB file:

1. encrypt.lu → relay.encrypt.lu → one PUT, ~<3 s, 200
2. privatenote.ai → upload.privatenote.ai → same shape (Bearer + XHR + Blob)

If (2) fails with ~200 ms `status: 0` and no Worker log: check CF on **upload host** (Bot Fight, WAF, Access) — curl OK + Safari large PUT silent is the usual Bot Fight signature.
If (2) works: staging zone/hop was the bug.

## Temporary chunking

`SAFARI_CHUNKING_ENABLED` defaults **false**. Re-enable only after prod same-site single PUT A/B fails and CF/CORS deltas are ruled out.
